From 7ef4e8fc14c1216f8f0f14f4b617332a2a2f7fae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Baricco <38298051+Baricco@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 14:53:28 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] fix false accepts: match ridges, not the sensor's fixed
 pattern

On the 27c6:5125 every frame carries a fixed pattern tied to the sensor
pixels (vertical stripes and blobs left by per-pixel gain and baseline).
In light presses it dominates the image, and since it sits on the same
pixels in every frame, SIFT keypoints of the pattern match those of any
other frame of any finger: on a 20 genuine / 20 impostor test set
impostors scored 2,000-13,000 against a threshold of 20, i.e. wrong
fingers were accepted.

- imgproc: new "ridge" pipeline, now the SIGFM default: raw - baseline in
  float, regression removal of the baseline-shaped gain residue, DoG
  band-pass on the ridge frequency (sigma 1/4 px), 1-99% stretch, CLAHE.
  The legacy pipeline stays available with GOODIX_IMGPROC_MODE=legacy.
- capture: a fresh no-finger frame right before arming finger detection
  becomes the baseline of the next press (discarded if it looks like a
  finger). Waiting for an image already requested is no longer
  cancellable: cancelling there left half a TLS record in the channel and
  every later image failed to decrypt (seen when libfprint deactivates
  between enroll stages).
- goodixgf: frames whose ridge contrast is below GOODIX_MIN_RIDGE
  (default 10; a full press is 100-200) are reported as retry instead of
  being enrolled or matched.

Measured live on a MateBook CREM-WXX9: 0/25 impostor presses accepted,
22/25 genuine presses accepted. That session also used the SIGFM fixes
that the last commit of this series applies; replaying the same frames
offline through the unpatched SIGFM gives the same counts.

